{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-334202" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution of the Clairaut differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+4({y}^{′})^{2}-{y}^{′}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14075964/state.json" "file_sha256" "1402529aa22cb6a529c1e8d51816dbc90d106b26c0746b35ea6ed851cd6959b8"} {"question" "q-334202" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve the Clairaut differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+4({y}^{′})^{2}-{y}^{′},\n$$\n\nwe start by setting\n$p={y}^{′}.$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation gives\n\n$$\ny=xp+4{p}^{2}-p.\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =(xp+4{p}^{2}-p)^{′} \\\\ p & =p+x{p}^{′}+8p{p}^{′}-{p}^{′} \\\\ 0 & ={p}^{′}(x+8p-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe product on the right-hand side equals zero, which means at least one of the factors must be zero.\n\nThe general solution of the Clairaut differential equation is obtained if ${p}^{′}=0.$ Then, $p$ is constant, say \n\n$$\np=c.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $p=c$ into $y=xp+4{p}^{2}-p,$ we get the general solution\n\n$$\ny=cx+4{c}^{2}-c.\n$$\n\nThis represents a family of straight lines, one line for each constant value of $c.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14075964/state.json" "file_sha256" "1402529aa22cb6a529c1e8d51816dbc90d106b26c0746b35ea6ed851cd6959b8"} {"question" "q-334202" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14075964/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "569a117973331f73f8ece6e91d0e32af87e11e8a9bb714c9ebb5ae7ff36c55f3"} {"question" "q-334202" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14075964/state.json" "file_sha256" "1402529aa22cb6a529c1e8d51816dbc90d106b26c0746b35ea6ed851cd6959b8"} {"question" "q-334202" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=4cx+{c}^{2}-c"] ["math" "y=cx+4{c}^{2}-c"] ["math" "y=cx+8{c}^{2}-c"] ["math" "y=cx+{c}^{2}-c"] ["math" "y={c}^{2}x+4{c}^{2}-c"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14075964/state.json" "file_sha256" "1402529aa22cb6a529c1e8d51816dbc90d106b26c0746b35ea6ed851cd6959b8"} {"question" "q-334202" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=cx+4{c}^{2}-c"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14075964/state.json" "file_sha256" "1402529aa22cb6a529c1e8d51816dbc90d106b26c0746b35ea6ed851cd6959b8"} {"question" "q-334203" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution of the Clairaut differential equation:\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+({y}^{′})^{3}-2{y}^{′}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14075964/state.json" "file_sha256" "1402529aa22cb6a529c1e8d51816dbc90d106b26c0746b35ea6ed851cd6959b8"} {"question" "q-334203" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve the Clairaut differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+({y}^{′})^{3}-2{y}^{′},\n$$\n\nwe start by setting\n$p={y}^{′}.$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation gives\n\n$$\ny=xp+{p}^{3}-2p.\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =(xp+{p}^{3}-2p)^{′} \\\\ p & =p+x{p}^{′}+3{p}^{2}{p}^{′}-2{p}^{′} \\\\ 0 & ={p}^{′}(x+3{p}^{2}-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe product on the right-hand side equals zero, which means at least one of the factors must be zero.\n\nThe general solution of the Clairaut differential equation is obtained if ${p}^{′}=0.$ Then, $p$ is constant, say \n\n$$\np=c.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $p=c$ into $y=xp+{p}^{3}-2p,$ we get the general solution\n\n$$\ny=cx+{c}^{3}-2c.\n$$\n\nThis represents a family of straight lines, one line for each constant value of $c.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14075964/state.json" "file_sha256" "1402529aa22cb6a529c1e8d51816dbc90d106b26c0746b35ea6ed851cd6959b8"} {"question" "q-334203" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14075964/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "569a117973331f73f8ece6e91d0e32af87e11e8a9bb714c9ebb5ae7ff36c55f3"} {"question" "q-334203" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14075964/state.json" "file_sha256" "1402529aa22cb6a529c1e8d51816dbc90d106b26c0746b35ea6ed851cd6959b8"} {"question" "q-334203" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=cx+2{c}^{3}-2c"] ["math" "y=cx+{c}^{2}-2c"] ["math" "y=cx+{c}^{3}-2c"] ["math" "y={c}^{2}x+{c}^{3}-2c"] ["math" "y={c}^{3}x+{c}^{3}-2c"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14075964/state.json" "file_sha256" "1402529aa22cb6a529c1e8d51816dbc90d106b26c0746b35ea6ed851cd6959b8"} {"question" "q-334203" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=cx+{c}^{3}-2c"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14075964/state.json" "file_sha256" "1402529aa22cb6a529c1e8d51816dbc90d106b26c0746b35ea6ed851cd6959b8"} {"question" "q-334210" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution of the Clairaut differential equation:\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+\\frac{1}{{y}^{′}},\\,{y}^{′}\\ne 0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14075964/state.json" "file_sha256" "1402529aa22cb6a529c1e8d51816dbc90d106b26c0746b35ea6ed851cd6959b8"} {"question" "q-334210" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve the Clairaut differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+\\frac{1}{{y}^{′}},\n$$\n\nwe start by setting\n$p={y}^{′}.$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation gives\n\n$$\ny=xp+\\frac{1}{p}.\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & ={(xp+\\frac{1}{p})}^{′} \\\\ p & =p+x{p}^{′}-\\frac{1}{{p}^{2}}{p}^{′} \\\\ 0 & ={p}^{′}(x-\\frac{1}{{p}^{2}})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe product on the right-hand side equals zero, which means at least one of the factors must be zero.\n\nThe general solution of the Clairaut differential equation is obtained if ${p}^{′}=0.$ Then, $p$ is constant, say \n\n$$\np=c,\n$$\n\nwith the restriction $c\\ne 0.$\n\nSubstituting $p=c$ into $y=xp+\\frac{1}{p},$ we get the general solution\n\n$$\ny=cx+\\frac{1}{c}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a family of straight lines, one line for each constant value of $c\\ne 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14075964/state.json" "file_sha256" "1402529aa22cb6a529c1e8d51816dbc90d106b26c0746b35ea6ed851cd6959b8"} {"question" "q-334210" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14075964/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "569a117973331f73f8ece6e91d0e32af87e11e8a9bb714c9ebb5ae7ff36c55f3"} {"question" "q-334210" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14075964/state.json" "file_sha256" "1402529aa22cb6a529c1e8d51816dbc90d106b26c0746b35ea6ed851cd6959b8"} {"question" "q-334210" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=cx+\\frac{1}{2c}"] ["math" "y=cx+\\frac{1}{c}"] ["math" "y=cx+c"] ["math" "y={c}^{2}x+\\frac{1}{c}"] ["math" "y={c}^{3}x+\\frac{1}{c}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14075964/state.json" "file_sha256" "1402529aa22cb6a529c1e8d51816dbc90d106b26c0746b35ea6ed851cd6959b8"} {"question" "q-334210" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=cx+\\frac{1}{c}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14075964/state.json" "file_sha256" "1402529aa22cb6a529c1e8d51816dbc90d106b26c0746b35ea6ed851cd6959b8"} {"question" "q-334453" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the singular solution to the following Clairaut differential equation:\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+\\sqrt{{y}^{′}},\\,{y}^{′}\\ge 0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14075964/state.json" "file_sha256" "1402529aa22cb6a529c1e8d51816dbc90d106b26c0746b35ea6ed851cd6959b8"} {"question" "q-334453" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A Clairaut differential equation has the form\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $g$ is a differentiable function of ${y}^{′}.$\n\nTo solve the Clairaut differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+\\sqrt{{y}^{′}},\n$$\n\nwe start by setting\n$p={y}^{′}.$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation gives\n\n$$\ny=xp+\\sqrt{p}.\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =(xp+\\sqrt{p})^{′} \\\\ p & =p+x{p}^{′}+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{p}}{p}^{′} \\\\ 0 & ={p}^{′}(x+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{p}})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe product on the right-hand side equals zero, so at least one factor must be zero.\n\nThe singular solution of the Clairaut differential equation is obtained if $x+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{p}}=0.$ Then,\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{p}}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute this into $y=xp+\\sqrt{p}\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =xp+\\sqrt{p} \\\\  & =(-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{p}})p+\\sqrt{p} \\\\  & =-\\frac{p}{2\\sqrt{p}}+\\sqrt{p} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{p}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the singular solution is given parametrically by\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{p}} \\\\ y=\\frac{\\sqrt{p}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo eliminate $p,$ we first solve the first equation for $\\sqrt{p}\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{p}=-\\frac{1}{2x}\n$$\n\nSince $x=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{p}},$ we must have $x<0.$\n\nNext, let's substitute this expression for $\\sqrt{p}$ into the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{\\sqrt{p}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{1}{2x})}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the explicit form of the singular solution is\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{4x},\\,x<0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14075964/state.json" "file_sha256" "1402529aa22cb6a529c1e8d51816dbc90d106b26c0746b35ea6ed851cd6959b8"} {"question" "q-334453" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14075964/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "569a117973331f73f8ece6e91d0e32af87e11e8a9bb714c9ebb5ae7ff36c55f3"} {"question" "q-334453" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14075964/state.json" "file_sha256" "1402529aa22cb6a529c1e8d51816dbc90d106b26c0746b35ea6ed851cd6959b8"} {"question" "q-334453" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-\\frac{1}{2x},\\,x<0"] ["math" "y=-\\frac{1}{4x},\\,x<0"] ["math" "y=-\\frac{1}{x},\\,x<0"] ["math" "y=-\\frac{1}{x},\\,x>0"] ["math" "y=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}},\\,x<0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14075964/state.json" "file_sha256" "1402529aa22cb6a529c1e8d51816dbc90d106b26c0746b35ea6ed851cd6959b8"} {"question" "q-334453" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=-\\frac{1}{4x},\\,x<0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14075964/state.json" "file_sha256" "1402529aa22cb6a529c1e8d51816dbc90d106b26c0746b35ea6ed851cd6959b8"} {"question" "q-334457" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the singular solution to the following Clairaut differential equation:\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{′}),\\,-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le {y}^{′}\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14075964/state.json" "file_sha256" "1402529aa22cb6a529c1e8d51816dbc90d106b26c0746b35ea6ed851cd6959b8"} {"question" "q-334457" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A Clairaut differential equation has the form\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $g$ is a differentiable function of ${y}^{′}.$\n\nTo solve the Clairaut differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwe start by setting\n$p={y}^{′}.$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation gives\n\n$$\ny=xp+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(p).\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =(xp+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(p))^{′} \\\\ p & =p+x{p}^{′}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(p){p}^{′} \\\\ 0 & ={p}^{′}(x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(p))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe product on the right-hand side equals zero, so at least one factor must be zero.\n\nThe singular solution of the Clairaut differential equation is obtained if $x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(p)=0.$ Then,\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(p).\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute this into $y=xp+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(p):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =xp+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(p) \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(p))p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(p) \\\\  & =p\\operatorname{sin}⁡(p)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(p)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the singular solution is given parametrically by\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(p) \\\\ y=p\\operatorname{sin}⁡(p)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(p)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo eliminate $p,$ we first solve the first equation for $p:$\n\n$$\np=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)\n$$\n\nThis is valid only for $-1\\le x\\le 1$ and $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le p\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\nNext, let's substitute this expression for $p$ into the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =p\\operatorname{sin}⁡(p)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(p) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)\\cdot x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)) \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the explicit form of the singular solution is\n\n$$\ny=x\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)),\\,-1\\le x\\le 1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14075964/state.json" "file_sha256" "1402529aa22cb6a529c1e8d51816dbc90d106b26c0746b35ea6ed851cd6959b8"} {"question" "q-334457" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14075964/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "569a117973331f73f8ece6e91d0e32af87e11e8a9bb714c9ebb5ae7ff36c55f3"} {"question" "q-334457" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14075964/state.json" "file_sha256" "1402529aa22cb6a529c1e8d51816dbc90d106b26c0746b35ea6ed851cd6959b8"} {"question" "q-334457" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)),\\,-1\\le x\\le 1"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)),\\,-1\\le x\\le 1"] ["math" "y=x\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)),\\,-1\\le x\\le 1"] ["math" "y=x\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)),\\,-1\\le x\\le 1"] ["math" "y={x}^{2}\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)),\\,-1\\le x\\le 1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14075964/state.json" "file_sha256" "1402529aa22cb6a529c1e8d51816dbc90d106b26c0746b35ea6ed851cd6959b8"} {"question" "q-334457" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=x\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)),\\,-1\\le x\\le 1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14075964/state.json" "file_sha256" "1402529aa22cb6a529c1e8d51816dbc90d106b26c0746b35ea6ed851cd6959b8"}] "usage" {"q-334202" []} "basis" 2765 "retractions" [[17592186217742 :question/problem "Find the general solution of the Clairaut differential equation\n\n$y = xy^{′} + 4(y^{′})^{2} - y^{′}$."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186216544 17592186216545 17592186216546 17592186216547 17592186216548] "immutable_fields" [[17592186216543 :answer-field/correct] [17592186216543 :answer-field/id] [17592186216543 :answer-field/key] [17592186216543 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
